## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- hi-a 1 and hi-a 8. The English column still says courts generally impose about 3 months (and about 4 / 6 months) and that the attorney should pursue the maximum compensation available. Those sentences were softened on purpose by R3. Putting “सामान्यतः” and “अधिकतम” back would make them read as a usual sentence and a compensation target. The softened Hindi is the form this campaign requires.
- The article-number, copyright-gloss, and lakh-grouping rows are not listed here. The reviewer is right about the URL (Article 3), about 著作權 beside 商標/專利, and about Indian grouping. They were skipped for the checker and the gloss-parity test, as above.
